<title>NETHERLANDS: FUGRO FINAL '96 NET JUMPS, DIV SHARPLY UP.</title>
<headline>FUGRO FINAL '96 NET JUMPS, DIV SHARPLY UP.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     3.07 vs   1.37 </p>
<p>    Net profit			    35.3  vs  15.8</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)		  1.50 vs   0.70 </p>
<p>    Turnover			     827.0  vs 653.7</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    57.1  vs  27.4</p>
<p>    Interest charges		     8.7  vs   9.7</p>
<p>    Tax				     11.6  vs   2.6</p>
<p>    Minorities charge		    1.6  vs   0.7 gain</p>
<p>NOTE - Engineering consultancy Fugro NV last month announced</p>
<p>a provisional 1996 net profit of about 35 million guilders or</p>
<p>3.05 guilders per share on a turnover of 820 million guilders.</p>
<p>Fugro said it was too early to give a profit forecast for</p>
<p>the current year, as many orders were given at short notice.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite favourable developments, we therefore refrain from</p>
<p>making a statement on turnover and profit expectations for 1997</p>
<p>until the release of our first half results,&quot; Fugro said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
